    "title": "Home Opener Set for Saturday for Wolves Women's Basketball - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By BVM Sportsdesk, ,\n7 hours ago The UWG women's basketball team is set to open their home season Saturday at 2 p.m. against Gardner-Webb after a challenging road trip. Both teams arrive winless, with West Georgia (0-1) narrowly losing to Oregon and Gardner-Webb (0-1) falling to Queens. The Wolves showcased resilience, with Jasmine Jones scoring 19 points against Oregon, while Gardner-Webb struggled offensively, scoring just 47 points in their opener. Head coach Joanna Reitz emphasized the need for a full 40-minute performance against a newly revamped Gardner-Webb team. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
